  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations to South Carolina totaled $9.1B in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 17,139 awards, with an average award size of $533K, and obligations were up 9.8% year over year. The Department of Energy is the largest buyer, obligating $4.8B, followed by the Department of Defense at $2.4B. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry by obligations at $3.7B, followed by Remediation Services at $1.1B. Major vendors include SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC at $3.4B and SAVANNAH RIVER MISSION COMPLETION, LLC at $1.1B. Fiscal-year history shows obligations moved from $6.7B in FY21 to $9.1B in FY26, with a peak of $10.6B in FY24 and $8.3B in FY25. These figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are the biggest buyers in South Carolina?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy is the largest buyer, obligating $4.8B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the second-largest buyer, obligating $2.4B. The Department of Health and Human Services, the Department of Homeland Security, and the Department of Veterans Affairs follow with $693M, $509M, and $329M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top contractors and which industries capture most obligations?",
        "body": "SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC and SAVANNAH RIVER MISSION COMPLETION, LLC lead vendors with $3.4B and $1.1B respectively. BRASFIELD & GORRIE LLC and PALMETTO GBA, LLC follow with $382M and $324M. Facilities Support Services and Remediation Services are the largest industries by obligations at $3.7B and $1.1B, with Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $880M and Engineering Services at $576M."
      }
    ]
  },
